SCOPE. This licence covers the original work in this repository: the logger
source, the host configuration under SystemSetup/, the offline tools under
Tools/, the hardware build sheet under Hardware/, the RaceChrono channel
definitions under RaceChrono/, and the documentation.

It does NOT cover bluez_inc, which is a git submodule rather than a copy: that
code is MIT licensed by Martijn van Welie and carries its own LICENSE in its own
repository. It also does not cover RaceChrono, BlueZ, Raspberry Pi OS or any
other dependency this project talks to or builds against.

NO WARRANTY OF FITNESS FOR VEHICLE USE. This repository documents a logger wired
to a car's constant 12 V supply and mounted in a wheel-well cavity, and its
Hardware/ build sheet is a set of instructions someone could follow. It is a
record of what was built for one car, not validated engineering advice, and it
has electrical, thermal and mechanical risk. Anyone building or fitting
something from it does so at their own risk and is responsible for their own
fusing, isolation, mounting and compliance with applicable road-use regulation.
